  "scientific_interpretation": [
    "The long-horizon V03 sign failures of R4, R5 and R6 are not confined to an arbitrary near-zero-flux neighborhood.",
    "At first mismatch the Reference bottom flux is about -0.992, -0.596 and -0.373 cm/d for R4, R5 and R6 respectively; the wrong-sign segments then persist to step 1024.",
    "R8, R12 and the R16 LARE control have no V03 sign mismatch, supporting C4V minimum R8 without introducing a deadband.",
    "The V04 one-step early reversal remains distinct: it occurs where the Reference flux is near zero and is retained only as timing context, not reclassified.",
    "C4W is descriptive mechanism context. It does not alter C4V, authorize closure retuning, set application tolerance, or admit production use."
  ],
